><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA TOSHIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAHISA MITSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UYAMA TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA, TOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAHISA, MITSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UYAMA, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flat battery comprising a battery case doubling as one electrode terminal, a sealing plate doubling as the other electrode terminal and consisting of a planar center portion projecting toward an outer face side and planar peripheral edges extending almost in parallel with the center portion, and a gasket insulating the case from the sealing plate and sealing a power generating element, characterized in that the peripheral edges of the sealing plate are bent at further outer peripheral edges, or the case has folding portions to be fitted to the peripheral edges of the sealing plate via the gasket, the folding portions partially compressing the gasket. The flat battery, with such an improved sealing plate and/or improved case shape, is excellent in electrolyte leakage resistance and mass-productivity despite its thin structure.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une batterie plate comportant une chemise de logement de batterie faisant office de borne d'électrode, une chemise de plaque d'étanchéité faisant office d'autre borne d'électrode et consistant en une partie centrale plane saillant vers un côté de face extérieure et des bords périphériques plans s'étendant principalement parallèlement à la partie centrale, et un joint isolant le boîtier de la plaque d'étanchéité et isolant un élément générateur de l'énergie, se caractérisant en ce que les bords périphériques de la plaque d'étanchéité sont courbés au niveau des bords périphériques extérieurs, ou que le boîtier présente des parties à adapter aux bords périphériques de la plaque d'étanchéité au moyen du joint, lequel est partiellement comprimé par les parties se pliant. La batterie plate, grâce à la plaque d'étanchéité améliorée et/ou à la forme du boîtier améliorée, présente des propriétés de résistance aux fuites d'électrolyte élevée et peut être produite en masse malgré sa structure mince.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>